@startuml
' Day 4 — Task 46: High-Level System Architecture (digitized)
' Hand-drawn original: docs/handwritten/day4-architecture.jpg (mandatory first)
' Rule: 2+ API instances behind a load balancer (a single-instance design fails);
' every arrow direction is meaningful; acknowledged SPOFs are stated.

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam nodeFontSize 12

actor "Employee App (mobile)" as EA
actor "Captain App (mobile)" as CA
actor "Manager Dashboard (web)" as DB
actor "Call Center Tool (web)" as CC
actor "Admin Console (web)" as AD

node "Load Balancer\n(HA pair)" as LB
node "API Instances\n(2..n)" as API
node "WebSocket Gateway\n(2..n)" as WS
database "PostgreSQL\n(primary + standby)" as PG
database "Redis\n(cache + Pub/Sub)" as REDIS
queue "Message Queue\n(worker pool)" as MQ
node "Notification Workers" as NW

EA --> LB : HTTPS
CA --> LB : HTTPS
DB --> LB : HTTPS
CC --> LB : HTTPS
AD --> LB : HTTPS

LB --> API : route REST
LB --> WS : route WS upgrade

API --> PG : read/write (source of truth)
API --> REDIS : cache (keyed by tenant)
API --> MQ : publish domain events
WS --> REDIS : subscribe to channels
WS --> API : catch-up reads on reconnect

MQ --> NW : deliver (at-least-once)
NW --> PG : write notifications / retries
NW --> REDIS : idempotency dedup

note bottom of API
  Horizontally scalable; NO instance-local state (NFR-005).
  Publisher and gateway are decoupled via Redis channels —
  an event reaches the client regardless of which instance
  handled the request (Task 23 / Task 55).
end note

note bottom of PG
  Single source of truth — the ONLY acknowledged SPOF,
  mitigated by standby replica + backups (NFR-007).
end note

note bottom of REDIS
  Transport and cache ONLY — never the source of truth.
  Outage => polling fallback, no data loss (NFR-008).
end note
@enduml
